WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.984
Raj: We lacked a negative test case. Fixtures always supplied a valid tenant identifier.

2
00:00:06.984 --> 00:00:15.553
Hannah: The reproduction establishes the direct path failure. Why review missed it still needs investigation.

3
00:00:15.553 --> 00:00:22.609
Priya: Okay, just to recap, reads are restored. Cleanup remains limited to the approved tenant.

4
00:00:22.609 --> 00:00:30.458
Anika: The guard clause covers missing arguments, right? Path containment also covers valid but unsafe paths.

5
00:00:30.458 --> 00:00:37.826
Lukas: Yes, plus scoped permissions and race protection. Don't collapse those layers into one checkbox.

6
00:00:37.826 --> 00:00:45.482
Raj: One action item is mutation-based safety testing. I'll prove disabled guards make tests fail.

7
00:00:45.482 --> 00:00:53.139
Hannah: I'll review that evidence before closure. Passing tests need to detect broken safeguards.

8
00:00:53.139 --> 00:00:59.547
Priya: Maybe we should sample other cleanup tools. Let's close the loop on this one first.

9
00:00:59.547 --> 00:01:06.700
Lukas: Assign a deadline for the review investigation. Recovery success doesn't explain the approval gap.

10
00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:13.540
Anika: I'll bring the evidence next Tuesday. Expansion stays blocked until the checks are signed off.

